+# Performance history
+
+Measured costs of hot-path operations over time. Only measured numbers go
+here; if a change wasn't benchmarked, this file says so instead of guessing.
+
+## SessionStart health gate
+
+The nine-check health gate (`crates/muninn-core/src/health.rs`) runs on every
+`SessionStart`. Its cost on a 5k-record store:
+
+| When | p50 | What changed |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Before | 11.9 ms | `quick_check` (`PRAGMA quick_check`, O(file size)) ran on the read path on every hook invocation. |
+| After | 1.05 ms | `quick_check` taken off the read path; its result is now recorded once (`db.rs::record_quick_check`) and read back in O(1). A trigger-maintained `fts_rows` counter replaced a live FTS/`record` count comparison, and a `CHECK` constraint on the body column replaced an application-side validation pass. |
+
+With `quick_check` off the read path, `live=false` callers (hooks) only
+consult O(1) evidence — the recorded `quick_check` outcome and `fts_rows` —
+so the gate cost stays under a millisecond regardless of store size; `live=true`
+(`muninn doctor`) still runs the checks for real. See the comment at
+`crates/muninn-core/src/health.rs:83-89`.
+
+These numbers come from a prior session's benchmark run (tool-observed,
+trust 1 in Muninn's own provenance scheme — corroborated by, but not
+independently re-run in, this session). They have not been re-measured here;
+treat the exact figures as historical record rather than a live guarantee for
+the current codebase.
